Subject: [PATCH] compositor: native XWayland hosting

Run X11 clients on y5's own Xwayland server instead of the xwayland-satellite
proxy. The compositor spawns the `Xwayland` binary and is that server's X11
window manager in-process (smithay's `xwayland` feature).

Held out of the vendor-refresh commit so it can be reviewed on its own. Apply
with `git apply` (or `patch -p1`) on top of the vendor refresh — it is written
against the UPDATED vendors, not the ones that were in tree when it was written.

WHAT IT CONTAINS
  - vendor/smithay: adds `X11Surface::set_input_focus`, the X11 half of keyboard
    focus (SetInputFocus + WM_TAKE_FOCUS, honouring the ICCCM input model).
    Needed because y5's `SeatHandler::KeyboardFocus` is the plain `WlSurface`, so
    smithay's `KeyboardTarget for X11Surface` — where a compositor with an enum
    focus target gets this for free — is never reached. Without it the X server
    is never told which window has focus and X clients get no keyboard input.
  - compositor.workspace: enables smithay's `xwayland` feature; two lint
    allowlist entries the feature's size pushes over the policy.
  - 5 new crates:
      state.xwayland/{xwayland.base,xwayland.factory,xwayland.display}
      state.window/{window.shell,window.kind}
  - kernel.loader/.../xwayland.rs: spawns the server, starts the X11 WM on a
    nested calloop loop, publishes DISPLAY on ready.
  - ~40 call sites converted from `.toplevel()` to the shell-agnostic facade.
  - installer: drops the xwayland-satellite build/install; CLAUDE.md section.

DESIGN NOTES
  - `XwmHandler` is implemented on `Dispatch`, not `Loop`: smithay's surface
    association is a wayland PRE-COMMIT hook typed on the dispatch state, so that
    shape is forced. It fits the existing rim/outbox split — X11 handlers stay
    world-free and record onto outboxes `Wire::drain_protocol` applies.
  - X11 windows are configured at their y5-WORLD location, because an X client
    places its own override-redirect children against the geometry we hand their
    parent. `last_configure` (not `geometry`, which has _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS
    subtracted) is what round-trips back into `configure`.
  - Every X11 window's wl_surface belongs to the one Xwayland client, so surface
    credentials name the X SERVER. The pid comes from `_NET_WM_PID`.

VERIFIED: 30/30 workspace roots compile with this applied; workspace lint clean.
NOT runtime-tested (needs a Wayland/DRM session).
